{
  "vocabulary": "aspects",
  "version": "1.2.0",
  "notes": [
    "Two aspect classes. 'attribute' = objective facts about what a product is, from structured metadata or seller-stated listing text. 'quality' = subjective judgements that may ONLY be supported by reviews.",
    "Every HAS_ASPECT edge records evidence_type: 'structured' (details/categories/domain) or 'listing_stated' (seller title/features). Listing-stated attributes are seller statements, not verified facts.",
    "Unverified seller quality claims ('durable', 'premium', 'safe', 'high quality') are never recorded in v1.",
    "Values used for filtering (page count, format, reading level, language, piece count, player count, battery type) stay on the Product node or in the corpus. They are not aspects.",
    "Confidence values are heuristic rule scores, not calibrated probabilities. An edge with several evidence items takes the max.",
    "Text matches are dropped when negated within their clause (e.g. 'not printed on wood', 'alternative to plastic') or when the material names packaging or finish rather than the product (e.g. 'velvet gift bag', 'satin clear coat').",
    "component_guard (material aspects): text matches inside counted kit-content lists (\"1 Plastic Funnel, 1 Wooden Stick, 1 Plastic Flask\") or marked as spare, replaced or not included (\"Cotton is not included\") are ignored. Cross-sell sentences in features are ignored for every aspect.",
    "Quality aspects take review_cues only. They are matched in review text by review_inference.py and never in listing text; listing rules on quality aspects are still rejected."
  ],
